      "index": 2,
      "id": "comp-kfofzl2n",
      "text": "Artists Lena Wolff and Michele Pred create artworks, projects and actions that contribute to the long work of democracy, public dialogue, and civic engagement through feminist activism and art. A collection of their visual works, from Lena's VOTE posters (30,000 currently being distributed across the country!) and textile pieces to a lit handbag and voting booth by Michele will fill Dream Farm Commons, as a site for actions and gathering in the crucial days before the election.The exhibition will be seen from the street, but we will have get out the vote actions every Saturday, October 10, 17, 24 & 31, 12-3PM, outdoors and socially distanced: local ballot teach in, postcarding, pick up of VOTE posters, phone calls to swing districts, action plan for the days leading up to the election, and more. If you have an idea bring it down! Or just come and convene and re-energize for the weeks to come. Generally phone, computer, pens, postcard stamps are useful.\nDrop us an email at info@dreamfarmcommons.com if you want to know other specifics or help with this activation",
      "html": "<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:17px; line-height:1.5em; text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"font-family:worksans-extralight,work sans,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#221F20;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0em;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:17px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Artists Lena Wolff and Michele Pred create artworks, projects and actions that&nbsp;contribute to the long work of democracy, public dialogue, and civic engagement through feminist activism and art.&nbsp;A collection of their visual works, from Lena's&nbsp;VOTE posters (30,000 currently being distributed across the country!) &nbsp;and textile pieces to a lit handbag &nbsp;and voting booth by Michele will fill Dream Farm Commons, as a site for actions and gathering in the crucial days before the election.The exhibition will be seen from the street, but we will have get out the vote actions every Saturday,&nbsp;October 10, 17, 24 &amp; 31, 12-3PM, outdoors and&nbsp;socially distanced: local ballot teach in,&nbsp;postcarding, pick up of VOTE posters, phone calls to swing districts,&nbsp;action plan for the days leading up to the election, and&nbsp;more. If you have an idea bring it down!&nbsp;Or just come and convene and re-energize for the weeks to come. Generally phone, computer, pens, postcard stamps are useful.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:17px; line-height:1.5em; text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:17px; line-height:1.5em; text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"font-family:worksans-extralight,work sans,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#221F20;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0em;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:17px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Drop us an email at <a data-auto-recognition=\"true\" href=\"mailto:info@dreamfarmcommons.com\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">info@dreamfarmcommons.com</a> if you want to know&nbsp;other specifics or help with this activation</span></span></span></span></p>",
      "sha256": "b518ce4f26bc08ed86941bbbbd8355f0613f8533e3879a186630e66f2eba6ba6"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "id": "comp-kfog71oh",
      "text": "Join us on the sidewalk and in the street\nSaturday October 10 3-5pm\nat 349 15th St Oakland\nRECEPTION + poster pick up and powering up for the final weeks before the election",
